---
name: sdlc-spec
description: Draft a feature spec (PRD and checks) from a requirements document (.pdf, .docx, .md or .txt). Type /sdlc-spec requirements.pdf.
argument-hint: requirements.pdf
disable-model-invocation: true
allowed-tools: Bash(./scripts/sdlc spec * --dry-run *) Bash(./scripts/sdlc implement * --dry-run *) Bash(git status *)
---

# /sdlc-spec $ARGUMENTS

Draft a specification from the requirements document `$ARGUMENTS`. **You are the agent; `./scripts/sdlc` reads the document and checks the draft.**
You write only the spec: no code, no tests, and no other file. On Windows PowerShell or cmd, write `.\scripts\sdlc.cmd` wherever this says `./scripts/sdlc`.

1. No document given: ask for its path and stop. It must exist and be a `.pdf`, `.docx`, `.md` or `.txt` file.
2. `git status --short` must print nothing: the tool wants a clean tree so that your draft is the only change. Otherwise ask the person to commit or stash first, and stop.
3. `./scripts/sdlc spec $ARGUMENTS --dry-run --agent claude` (quote the path if it has spaces) creates nothing and starts no agent. It reads the document, then prints
   `would create: .ai/specs/FEAT-00N-<name>/` and `prompt: .ai/evidence/<run>/spec.prompt.md`. If the document describes several features, ask which one this is for, and add
   `--focus "<that part>" --name <slug>` to the command.
4. Create the folder it named and copy the source document into its `source/` subfolder (the CLI does that itself). Then **read the prompt file whole and do what it says**:
   it names the two files to write, their format, and the rules (every criterion cites the part of the document it comes from; gaps are listed as ASSUMPTIONS).
   One thing changes because you can talk to the person: where it says to write questions to a file and stop, ask the person here and wait.
5. Validate: `./scripts/sdlc implement FEAT-00N --dry-run --agent claude` runs nothing and must report `spec ok`. If it lists problems, fix the files and run it again,
   up to three times; then stop and show what is still wrong.
6. Report: how many acceptance criteria and checks you wrote, every ASSUMPTION, and every open question. Say clearly that this is a **draft written by an AI**: the person
   compares it with the document, confirms or changes each ASSUMPTION, sets `Status: Accepted`, and only then runs `/sdlc-implement FEAT-00N`. Do not implement anything.
